# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with an idle keepalive.
#
# The harness runs the image CMD so services actually boot. The CMD is
# PID-1-safe:
#   * sshd + WinRM are started first;
#   * MariaDB and IIS (W3SVC) are started via Start-Service, so both run under
#     the Windows service host (services.exe), NOT PID 1;
#   * PID 1 is an idle `while ($true) { Start-Sleep 60 }` loop.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the WordPress site is ALREADY SERVING against a
# live MariaDB with the weak admin:admin credential, so a fix must rotate the
# WP admin password in MariaDB (safe now - neither service is PID 1) while
# keeping the site reachable. Restarting a service can never kill the container.
